  "interpretation": "Both north-up photographs place the rounded copper crown southwest of the OSM point. Both show an elongated light feature across the north side of the church at the OSM point. Its roof, wall faces and shadows are not separable as a four-corner ground footprint. The existing model crown top is displaced relative to its registered vertical axis by several metres in both images. The possible square dark feature on the river side of the dome is outside the northeast search quadrant. It is not adopted as the tower. Photo evidence and the parish account link the freestanding belfry to this side of the church, but the OSM node itself has only man_made=tower. Use independent ground-photo tower base corners and their errors before deciding whether to add it to the ordinary map. The former church, its yard clipping and all other owners remain unchanged."
